WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:03.667
-Welcome to the show.
-Thank you for having me.

00:00:03.667 --> 00:00:05.501
-It is --
It is great to have you on.

00:00:05.501 --> 00:00:07.567
I'm a big fan. I --
-Me too. I must say...

00:00:07.567 --> 00:00:09.100
-Yeah.
-...it's particularly nice

00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:11.734
to be on because I've got
a soft spot for the show.

00:00:11.734 --> 00:00:14.234
One of my kids, a few years ago,
sent me a clip

00:00:14.234 --> 00:00:17.133
of you and Bradley Cooper

00:00:17.133 --> 00:00:19.467
irretrievably breaking --
breaking up.

00:00:19.467 --> 00:00:21.167
-Laughing so hard.
-Like, yeah.

00:00:21.167 --> 00:00:22.734
-That was --
We cut that down actually.

00:00:22.734 --> 00:00:24.434
-It's just joyful.
Well, the whole segment.

00:00:24.434 --> 00:00:26.467
-The whole segment? Well,
we actually even cut that down.

00:00:26.467 --> 00:00:28.367
-You walked away at one point.
-We laughed for 25 minutes.

00:00:28.367 --> 00:00:30.801
It was terrible.
It was very unprofessional.

00:00:30.801 --> 00:00:33.367
-There's one moment, you're --
you're on the floor, face down.

00:00:33.367 --> 00:00:34.868
-I'm wiping my tears.
-Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:00:34.868 --> 00:00:37.167
-He's not --
He's banned from the show.

00:00:37.167 --> 00:00:38.868
Yeah, he actually is.
Not allowed back.

00:00:38.868 --> 00:00:40.434
-Good. Ban him.
-Yeah, and we only have

00:00:40.434 --> 00:00:42.200
professional actors now
on the show.

00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:44.234
-Yeah, this is -- yeah.
-You went to a very prestigious

00:00:44.234 --> 00:00:47.701
drama school in the
Royal Academy of Dramatic Art

00:00:47.701 --> 00:00:49.334
in London.
-I did. A long time ago, yeah.

00:00:49.334 --> 00:00:51.033
-Yes. We actually
found your headshot...

00:00:51.033 --> 00:00:52.200
-Did you?

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:53.767
-...from when you were
in that -- Yeah.

00:00:53.767 --> 00:00:55.634
Tell me about this guy.
What was he all about?

00:00:55.634 --> 00:00:57.334
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:57.334 --> 00:01:00.634
Wow. Wow.

00:01:00.634 --> 00:01:04.300
-I look -- I look like
a sort of nervous Tarzan.

00:01:04.300 --> 00:01:06.501
I look like a weird --
And there's some sideburns...

00:01:06.501 --> 00:01:07.734
-Yeah.
-...going on there.

00:01:07.734 --> 00:01:09.300
-I like his vibe.
I like his style.

00:01:09.300 --> 00:01:10.300
He's like --
-Yeah.

00:01:10.300 --> 00:01:11.868
-He -- He was --
He was going out.

00:01:11.868 --> 00:01:13.467
He wanted to get hired
for anything?

00:01:13.467 --> 00:01:15.133
What was he wanting to do?
-Yeah.

00:01:15.133 --> 00:01:18.234
It's a bit like, "Pick me.
Not -- Don't really pick me."

00:01:18.234 --> 00:01:20.133
-"Pick me, but don't."
-"Don't -- Yeah."

00:01:20.133 --> 00:01:21.767
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:01:21.767 --> 00:01:23.100
-Did -- This is --

00:01:23.100 --> 00:01:25.167
Did it feel like you were
going to nail it at the time?

00:01:25.167 --> 00:01:26.434
Did you go,
"Yeah, I've got this"?

00:01:26.434 --> 00:01:27.701
-No. No.

00:01:27.701 --> 00:01:29.834
Just terror. Just total
uncertainty and terror.

00:01:29.834 --> 00:01:32.901
It never -- It doesn't
really end, that feeling.

00:01:32.901 --> 00:01:34.367
-This guy went --

00:01:34.367 --> 00:01:38.033
This guy went to win numerous
awards for "Succession."

00:01:38.033 --> 00:01:40.067
I mean, come on.
He's beloved now.

00:01:40.067 --> 00:01:42.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:42.300 --> 00:01:46.601
BAFTA. BAFTA winner.
Not too shabby.

00:01:46.601 --> 00:01:48.567
I mean, multiple,
multiple awards.

00:01:48.567 --> 00:01:50.901
I mean, has this --
has this gone to your head?

00:01:50.901 --> 00:01:53.567
-Uh, no, it's sort of -- No.

00:01:53.567 --> 00:01:55.234
It's very nice. It's very nice.

00:01:55.234 --> 00:01:57.200
The Emmy --
The Emmy night was very scary.

00:01:57.200 --> 00:01:59.634
-Why? Just --
-Just 'cause you're sort of

00:01:59.634 --> 00:02:02.133
normalizing everything all
the time and trying not to be --

00:02:02.133 --> 00:02:03.501
You know,
'cause there's Ben Stiller

00:02:03.501 --> 00:02:05.767
and there's Oprah Winfrey,
and you're trying to

00:02:05.767 --> 00:02:07.667
make it normal, and actually
it's just horrifying.

00:02:07.667 --> 00:02:09.601
-Yeah. How does -- how does --
-Really scary and --

00:02:09.601 --> 00:02:10.767
-How does the cast deal with you

00:02:10.767 --> 00:02:12.467
now that you're
a multiple award winner?

00:02:12.467 --> 00:02:14.467
-They don't speak to me anymore,
which is fine.

00:02:14.467 --> 00:02:16.400
They don't -- Yeah, yeah.
No, they're lovely.

00:02:16.400 --> 00:02:18.133
They're lovely.
-Yeah? They do? Yeah.

00:02:18.133 --> 00:02:21.267
How did you come up
with the voice of Tom?

00:02:21.267 --> 00:02:24.234
Because we all noticed
you're not American.

00:02:24.234 --> 00:02:26.334
-Well, yeah.
I'm not an American.

00:02:26.334 --> 00:02:28.400
-No. That gets the award
right there.

00:02:28.400 --> 00:02:30.334
[ Cheers and applause ]
That gets the award.

00:02:30.334 --> 00:02:31.868
Unbelievable.
-Yeah.

00:02:31.868 --> 00:02:33.601
It's really -- It's difficult.

00:02:33.601 --> 00:02:35.934
Sarah Snook, who's Australian,
who plays Shiv,

00:02:35.934 --> 00:02:38.033
she and I have sort of
accent days where we're like,

00:02:38.033 --> 00:02:39.934
"We can't do this.
We just can't do it."

00:02:39.934 --> 00:02:41.400
Everything sounds weird.

00:02:41.400 --> 00:02:43.868
"New York" is very hard to say
in an American accent.

00:02:43.868 --> 00:02:45.567
-How -- "New York"?

00:02:45.567 --> 00:02:47.467
-Yeah, it just kind of
turns into sort of

00:02:47.467 --> 00:02:48.968
"New Yarrrk. Nyork. N'york."

00:02:48.968 --> 00:02:50.400
It's like a whole --

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:52.234
Like, it's really --
Like, it's really hard.

00:02:52.234 --> 00:02:53.467
-"Let's go -- go to Nyork."

00:02:53.467 --> 00:02:55.567
-"Yeah, going to Nyork."
-"Let's go to Nyork."

00:02:55.567 --> 00:02:57.033
-"I'm an American,
and I go to Nyork.

00:02:57.033 --> 00:02:58.901
-"Live from Nyork,
it's 'Saturday Nert.'"

00:02:58.901 --> 00:03:00.934
-That's right.
But there are certain --

00:03:00.934 --> 00:03:02.601
If I look --
But if I look at the --

00:03:02.601 --> 00:03:04.267
If I look at Nick Braun,
who plays Greg,

00:03:04.267 --> 00:03:06.567
I suddenly think,
"Oh, there's Greg."

00:03:06.567 --> 00:03:08.968
And it's all -- it's just --

00:03:08.968 --> 00:03:11.400
Yeah, his sort of face
tells me what to do.

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:15.100
And my voice goes very high with
Sarah, partly through fear --

00:03:15.100 --> 00:03:17.167
Tom's fear of shiv.
-Yeah, of course.

00:03:17.167 --> 00:03:19.033
-So I start -- Yeah.
It's sort of --

00:03:19.033 --> 00:03:22.367
It's very like, "Honey, honey,
honey, no, no. Alright."

00:03:22.367 --> 00:03:25.834
And so then I sort of
find my level, yeah.

00:03:25.834 --> 00:03:27.100
-Well done.

00:03:27.100 --> 00:03:29.000
I want to talk about your
new miniseries on Britbox.

00:03:29.000 --> 00:03:31.300
Britbox, by the way, you can
download on anything you have.

00:03:31.300 --> 00:03:33.934
Apple TV or whatever it is.
It's a streaming service.

00:03:33.934 --> 00:03:36.167
This is based on a true story.

00:03:36.167 --> 00:03:38.767
Anyone who's not familiar
with John Stonehouse,

00:03:38.767 --> 00:03:40.133
can you set this up?

00:03:40.133 --> 00:03:42.200
-So, John Stonehouse
was a British M.P.,

00:03:42.200 --> 00:03:44.501
a Member of Parliament,
in the '60s and '70s,

00:03:44.501 --> 00:03:47.767
and he was kind of a rising star
in the Labour Party in Britain.

00:03:47.767 --> 00:03:52.033
And through various
unfortunate events,

00:03:52.033 --> 00:03:55.734
he has a terrible,
complicated love life

00:03:55.734 --> 00:03:59.100
and he gets in terrible
financial trouble.

00:03:59.100 --> 00:04:03.734
And he's spying, badly,
for the Czech secret service.

00:04:03.734 --> 00:04:06.033
And, anyway -- And it all
becomes too much for him.

00:04:06.033 --> 00:04:07.901
And he decides
to fake his own death.

00:04:07.901 --> 00:04:09.767
-So he fakes his own death.
-Yeah, he leaves his wife

00:04:09.767 --> 00:04:11.801
and children and he flies
to Miami on a business trip,

00:04:11.801 --> 00:04:13.934
on a so-called "business trip,"
and he swims --

00:04:13.934 --> 00:04:16.033
leaves his clothes on the beach
and a passport

00:04:16.033 --> 00:04:18.834
on top of his clothes
and swims into the sea.

00:04:18.834 --> 00:04:21.868
And then swims along
the coast a bit and comes out

00:04:21.868 --> 00:04:24.400
and then flies to Australia.
-Yeah. Oh, Australia?

00:04:24.400 --> 00:04:27.367
-On a fake -- with a fake
passport with a new identity.

00:04:27.367 --> 00:04:29.634
In the days when it was easier
to fake your own death,

00:04:29.634 --> 00:04:32.434
he does it.
-Yeah, yeah, if -- We all know.

00:04:32.434 --> 00:04:34.667
We all can relate to that.
Yeah, of course, yeah.

00:04:34.667 --> 00:04:36.901
-So -- And I didn't know
anything about this guy.

00:04:36.901 --> 00:04:39.767
So it was just a fascinating,
bonkers story.

00:04:39.767 --> 00:04:41.234
-Yeah.
-Amazing.

00:04:41.234 --> 00:04:43.734
-Your wife in real life,
Keeley Hawes,

00:04:43.734 --> 00:04:45.968
plays your wife in the show.
-Yeah.

00:04:45.968 --> 00:04:47.968
-Is that difficult to do or...?

00:04:47.968 --> 00:04:49.534
-It was lovely.
-It was great?

00:04:49.534 --> 00:04:51.167
-It was lovely, yeah.
It was really good.

00:04:51.167 --> 00:04:52.634
It was so nice.
-Yeah.

00:04:52.634 --> 00:04:54.868
-I mean, yeah, they have
an odd relationship in the show,

00:04:54.868 --> 00:04:57.334
and she sort of sees through
his shenanigans.

00:04:57.334 --> 00:04:59.868
But it was just great to play.
It was nice.

00:04:59.868 --> 00:05:03.801
Well, you said before
that your kids have never --

00:05:03.801 --> 00:05:05.834
no real want to see --

00:05:05.834 --> 00:05:08.167
-Desire to see us
on screen, ever.

00:05:08.167 --> 00:05:10.234
Not really.
-But even --

00:05:10.234 --> 00:05:12.400
even after the awards that
you've gotten and everything?

00:05:12.400 --> 00:05:14.534
-Not really. No.
-But then you said,

00:05:14.534 --> 00:05:16.434
"Well, maybe when they're
teenagers, they'll get into it."

00:05:16.434 --> 00:05:17.667
-That's what I thought.
-Yes.

00:05:17.667 --> 00:05:19.033
-Yeah, no.

00:05:19.033 --> 00:05:20.667
-They are teenagers.
-They are.

00:05:20.667 --> 00:05:22.501
-And they still don't.
-They're like 18 and 16.

00:05:22.501 --> 00:05:23.901
And they --
they have other things to watch.

00:05:23.901 --> 00:05:25.300
-What do they watch?

00:05:25.300 --> 00:05:27.033
-There's a lot of --
There's a lot -- Other stuff.

00:05:27.033 --> 00:05:28.467
I don't know, yeah.
-Anything but you.

00:05:28.467 --> 00:05:29.901
They don't want
to see Mom and Dad.

00:05:29.901 --> 00:05:31.300
-Not really.
-No, okay, yeah.

00:05:31.300 --> 00:05:32.701
Well, they should watch
"Stonehouse"

00:05:32.701 --> 00:05:34.334
because Mom and Dad
are really good in it.

00:05:34.334 --> 00:05:36.033
-Thank you.
-I just want to say that, yeah.

00:05:36.033 --> 00:05:39.367
Please watch -- Download Britbox
and get watching.

00:05:39.367 --> 00:05:41.234
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:05:41.234 --> 00:05:44.667
Here's Matthew Macfadyen and
Keeley Hawes in "Stonehouse."

00:05:44.667 --> 00:05:46.300
Take a look at this.

00:05:46.300 --> 00:05:52.634
♪♪

00:05:52.634 --> 00:05:59.000
♪♪

00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:01.334
-What are you doing?

00:06:01.334 --> 00:06:07.067
♪♪

00:06:07.067 --> 00:06:09.834
-It's private.

00:06:09.834 --> 00:06:14.100
-I -- I thought we didn't have
secrets from one another.

00:06:17.734 --> 00:06:20.067
-It's something
for your birthday.

00:06:22.501 --> 00:06:25.701
-But that's...two months away.

00:06:25.701 --> 00:06:30.434
♪♪

00:06:30.434 --> 00:06:31.567
Hm.

00:06:31.567 --> 00:06:33.701
♪♪

00:06:33.701 --> 00:06:37.901
-That's how you do it. Come on.
Matthew Macfadyen, everybody.

00:06:37.901 --> 00:06:41.834
"Stonehouse" premieres
on Britbox January 17th.

00:06:41.834 --> 00:06:44.567
We'll be right back with
